  "DescIdentified": {
    "type": "cexolocstring",
    "value": {
      "0": "The bowmen at Helm's Deep pass this wrap down to whoever draws sentry duty on the causeway -- it eases the tongue in council and steadies the nerve through long, cold watches. Its owner speaks a little more freely, and endures a little more, than the wool alone would explain."
    }
  },
  "Description": {
    "type": "cexolocstring",
    "value": {
      "0": "Rough-spun wool in a dull olive hue, this cloak smells of damp earth and pine resin. It muffles the sound of footsteps against the stone and stays close to the skin against the biting mountain wind."
    }
  },
